LibreQuake @VERSION@ for AmigaOS 3.x (AmiCradle)
=================================================

LibreQuake is a free and open replacement for Quake's data: its own maps,
monsters, textures, models and sounds, playable with any Quake engine. This
drawer is LibreQuake 0.09-beta (the "lite" set) with Quake 2.30 for the
Amiga, so it is a whole game with nothing else to find: no id Software
data is needed. Status: TESTING, not a release.

Requirements
------------

- AmigaOS 3.x, a 68040 or 68060 with an FPU, AGA or an RTG board.
- 16 MB of free Fast RAM for the game (quake -mem N for another size);
  the largest LibreQuake map, lq_e0m2, fits in it.
- AHI for the sound.

Installing and playing
----------------------

Unpack the archive where you keep games (lha x librequake-...lha Games:)
and double-click the quake icon, or from a Shell: cd to the drawer, then
quake. The menu's SOLO starts the episode. ` opens the console; the
PC version's keys, and the mouse turns. ENV:ACGame/Display set to AGA or
RTG chooses the screen.

This is the same Quake 2.30 program as the Quake drawer (DalsinAI/
amigaquake): drawn with Quake's C code, no CD audio and no network play
yet. LibreQuake's music (Ogg Vorbis tracks) is left out, as this Quake
has no music player; LibreQuake also asks for one sound it does not ship
(sound/player/slimbrn2.wav), which the console mentions.

